Links 2.30 for PsiLinux (links -g on the Psion's X desktop). Applied by ports/build-links.sh.
Built with -DPSILINUX; TLS through mbossl (ports/links/mbossl: OpenSSL's API over Mbed TLS).
- default.c, setup.h (PSILINUX): defaults for 640x240 in 16 greys and ~9 MB: 512 KB picture
  cache, 1 MB memory cache, 256 KB font cache, 2 formatted pages, 4 connections (2 a host),
  no async DNS (fork is a snapshot vfork), 15 px text, 14 px menus, white pages, flat greys
  for the menus and scroll bars (n * 0x11 and in Links' 6x6x6 cube), letters not dithered
- links.h, https.c (MBOSSL): the certificate check is Mbed TLS's, done in the handshake
  (chain, dates, name); verify_ssl_certificate asks mbossl for the outcome and the issuers;
  no built-in certificate store (the system's bundle is read on demand)
- links.h, default.c, sched.c, http.c, url.c, menu.c: option https_via_http_proxy
  (Setup > Network options > Proxies, "https:// through the HTTP proxy (it does the
  TLS)"): with an HTTP proxy such as PsiProxy set, https:// pages are asked of it
  as "GET https://..." instead of through CONNECT, so the proxy does the TLS (and can
  slim the page) and the Psion makes no handshake. Off by default; no proxy is built in.
- html.c, html_r.c, html_tbl.c (PSIWEB, PSI_STRIKES: PsiWeb's hunks unchanged): links
  underlined (blue is all but black in 16 greys); no "Link: canonical/alternate" lines and
  no prefetches; the parser's fast paths and the form search that is no longer quadratic
  (big pages on a 36 MHz ARM); list bullets from the hinted font
- jpeg.c (PSI_JPEG_SCALE, PsiWeb's hunk unchanged; on with PSILINUX): libjpeg scales by n/8
  to near the size shown, colour JPEGs decoded as grey, buffered-image mode only for
  progressive JPEGs, which take in all their data before a scan is shown
- links.h, dither.c, x.c (PSILINUX): grey mode. On an 8-bit PseudoColor visual (the Psion's
  X server, shown in 16 greys), Links allocates 31 greys in the default colour map (the 16
  levels and the halfway greys, which the Psion shows as an even checker) and draws in
  them: plain colours become their Rec.601 grey, as the Psion makes them, and pictures
  are dithered once (Floyd-Steinberg in light) instead of into the 6x6x6 cube that the
  Psion would dither again. No private colour map to install. LINKS_COLOUR=1: as before.
- dip.c (PSIWEB, PSI_STRIKES: PsiWeb's hunk unchanged), links.h, html_r.c: text
  from hinted DejaVu strikes pre-rendered at the cell heights drawn for the 15 px body
  size (ports/links/mkstrike.py), Links' masters (mkfont.py, run-length) otherwise; the
  glyph and picture scalers without divisions or soft float; glyph and width caches; the
  page's base size tells dip.c when the strikes apply (html_r.c)
- default.c, main.c, x.c (PSILINUX): with $DISPLAY set, links is the graphical browser
  without -g (psiwm's Web entry runs plain "links"; -no-g for text mode); the window
  starts as big as the screen (psiwm then fits it to its workspace); session.c: the
  window's title is the page's alone (psiwm's toolbar already says Links)
- bfu.c (PSILINUX): on a screen under 400 pixels high, a dialog's label and field share a
  line where both fit, with half the gap after them: Links cannot scroll a dialog, and
  the taller ones (Proxies, Cache, ...) were cut off at 240 pixels

